# Enterprise Design Principles

Implement using a modular, event-driven architecture with strongly typed domain models. Maintain backward compatibility with existing APIs while extending them to include ownership metadata. Ensure every dashboard, report, API response, AI explanation, remediation workflow, and exported report consumes the same normalized ownership model so the platform remains internally consistent.

---

# Success Criteria

This enhancement is complete when QGuard Helix no longer behaves like a traditional vulnerability scanner that merely identifies cryptographic issues. Instead, it should function as an enterprise-grade **Quantum Migration Decision Platform** that clearly distinguishes between customer-controlled, provider-controlled, and ecosystem-dependent findings, explains ownership and remediation responsibility for every issue, prioritizes only actionable work, integrates these concepts into dashboards, reports, Sophia™, migration planning, and Quantum Trust Certification™, and provides organizations with a realistic, dependency-aware roadmap toward post-quantum readiness.

